6. Vaultwarden 1.37.5 source code
   Files:       the Rust ported from Vaultwarden's, each named in a header comment in the file:
                - crates/kemlock-api-bw/src/sends.rs, from src/api/core/sends.rs (the handler and
                  helper structure, the update order, and the constants SEND_INACCESSIBLE_MSG and
                  SIZE_525_MB)
                - crates/kemlock-api-bw/src/cipher.rs, from src/db/models/cipher.rs
                  (Cipher::to_json), src/api/core/ciphers.rs (update_cipher_from_data) and
                  src/util.rs (lcase_first, process_json_key, get_display_size)
                - crates/kemlock-vaultwarden/src/cipher_json.rs, from src/db/models/cipher.rs
                  (Cipher::to_json) and src/util.rs (lcase_first, process_json_key)
                - crates/kemlock-vaultwarden/src/vwtime.rs (display_size), from src/util.rs
                  (get_display_size)
                - crates/kemlock-app/src/two_step/data.rs (EmailData, obscure_email), from
                  src/api/core/two_factor/email.rs (EmailTokenData, obscure_email)
                - crates/kemlock-api-bw/src/identity.rs (check_is_some and the grant dispatch in
                  token()), from src/api/identity.rs (login)
   Source:      https://github.com/dani-garcia/vaultwarden/tree/1.37.5 (the paths above are
                relative to it)
   Authors:     Daniel Garcia and the Vaultwarden contributors
   Licence:     GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 (AGPL-3.0; Vaultwarden's Cargo.toml
                says AGPL-3.0-only), the licence of this repository
   Changes:     rewritten onto Kemlock's model (its stores, ports and error types, no Rocket or
                Diesel); the parts named keep Vaultwarden's structure and behaviour.

